{"title":"2005 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 12B Problems\">2005 AMC 12B #3</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems\">2005 AMC 10B #5</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Brianna is using part of the money she earned on her weekend job to buy several equally-priced CDs. She used one fifth of her money to buy one third of the CDs. What fraction of her money will she have left after she buys all the CDs? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39fd5b0459b8073fe36d2f8ff63543c117c9be20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\ \\frac15 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) }\\ \\frac13 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) }\\ \\frac25 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) }\\ \\frac23 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) }\\ \\frac45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"403\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/8/628cf4cacc16de2b341c2ebd1abea7084569c8d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m =$\" width=\"34\" height=\"8\" /> Brianna's money.  We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5af09432d01b67af9ae696f495f50fd0fc945de0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac15 m = \\frac13 (\\mbox{CDs}) \\Rightarrow \\frac35 m = (\\mbox{CDs})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"237\" height=\"37\" />.  Thus, the money left over is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/f/60f8d58629cc9f8780ed8f8fdf538e4f113ad08f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m-\\frac35m = \\frac25m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"120\" height=\"37\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/e/55e77bf2b972186d3c0648aea28bf5d3f381f382.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{2}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"61\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>This was just a simple manipulation of the equation. No solving was needed!\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B\">2005 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a hre